WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.047 --> 00:00:08.592
Oh. Riiick...

2
00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:12.804
You were right. Morty.

3
00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:17.851
Chili... was too... spicy.

4
00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:21.188
Ohhh...
Ah.

5
00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.190
Oh.

6
00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:29.780
Estate sale is open!

7
00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:32.115
Getcha post-its out.
first come. first serve.

8
00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:33.367
If you see a post-it.

9
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.910
the item has
already been claimed.

10
00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:36.554
-Oh. yeah.
-Alright.

11
00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.121
Hey. nice office chair.

12
00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:39.873
Hatchi-Matchi.

13
00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:41.375
Pretty ghoulish.
don't you think?

14
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:43.335
W-we just get to
take anything we want?

15
00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.897
Morty. they're dead. You want to
be buried with your porn magazines?

16
00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:47.172
Magazines?

17
00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:49.091
W-what's a magazines. old man?

18
00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.218
Fuck you. Morty.
Go practice your pronouns.

19
00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.178
Whoa!

20
00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.556
An in-ground
two-post vehicle lift?

21
00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:57.808
You could park a motorcycle
on this bad boy

22
00:00:57.849 --> 00:00:59.518
and rotate it any which way.

23
00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:02.104
-I put my post-it on it first.
-No. no. I did!

24
00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:03.355
I come from a water planet.

25
00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:04.648
I should get the snorkel.

26
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:05.899
If you're from a water planet.

27
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:07.442
why do you need a snorkel?

28
00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:14.366
These estate sales
are lame af. am I right?

29
00:01:14.408 --> 00:01:15.158
Yeah.

30
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.368
I came to funeral hop.

31
00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:17.720
but there aren't any Smiths left

32
00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.079
to hold a funeral.

33
00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:20.080
Wait. funeral hop?

34
00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.206
Oh. shit.

35
00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.624
You gotta try it. dude.

36
00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:25.043
Some version of your mom.

37
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.628
your dad. bawling their eyes out

38
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.630
and saying the <i>nicest</i> shit
you've ever heard.

39
00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:30.340
But... can't happen when
the whole family

40
00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:31.717
checks out at the same time.

41
00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.052
Your Rick brings you
to your own funerals?

42
00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.430
Nah. dawg.
I drive myself.

43
00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:39.016
Whoa.
You don't got a Portal Jr.?

44
00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:40.392
Shit. bunch of us have one.

45
00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:42.311
Let's see. I bet...

46
00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:44.646
Bam.

47
00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:46.023
Pop a post-it on that bad boy

48
00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:47.399
before someone else does.

49
00:01:47.441 --> 00:01:48.317
Thanks.

50
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.735
And. uh. c-cool sunglasses.

51
00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:51.737
Sunglasses?

52
00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.821
These are my eyes.

53
00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:03.165
Um. Rick.

54
00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:04.583
you ever gone
to your own funeral?

55
00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:06.209
Is that new slang
for taking a dump?

56
00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.419
What? No.

57
00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:08.754
Well. I'm gonna start using it.

58
00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.023
Look. a Morty at the estate sale

59
00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:11.506
was a funeral hopper. and...

60
00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.067
Ugh. you can do better than
getting emotional handjobs

61
00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:14.092
from a fake family.

62
00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.510
My real family is dead.

63
00:02:15.594 --> 00:02:17.346
Wow. what a zing.
So is mine.

64
00:02:17.429 --> 00:02:19.848
The only thing that helps
ease the horror of existence

65
00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:21.600
is friction-free rotation.

66
00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:24.811
Did you buy a motorcycle
to justify the platform?

67
00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:26.396
Morty. <i>it turns.</i>

68
00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:28.482
C'mon. man.
I'm asking for guidance.

69
00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:30.817
Do whatever you want.
It's your funeral.

70
00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:48.502
Thank you.

71
00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:51.755
Big Legs Morty
loved Ritchie Valens.

72
00:02:51.797 --> 00:02:54.174
And now his Big Legs Grandfather

73
00:02:54.257 --> 00:02:55.467
is gonna say a few words.

74
00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.178
What!
Let me grieve!

75
00:02:58.261 --> 00:02:59.513
You've been drunk all week.

76
00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.390
<i>Maybe</i> if you had been sober.

77
00:03:01.473 --> 00:03:03.016
you wouldn't have
microwaved him.

78
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.310
His big legs were wet!

79
00:03:05.394 --> 00:03:06.770
I should have guessed.

80
00:03:06.812 --> 00:03:08.480
Wait! Big Legs Morty.

81
00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:11.233
I should have done this
when you were alive.

82
00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.654
Oh. hell yeah!

83
00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:58.572
Well. I guess
this is gonna be hard.

84
00:03:58.655 --> 00:04:00.449
but Mort loved
to do hard things.

85
00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.617
So...
we're gonna do this for him.

86
00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:06.872
How many of you here
<i>loved</i> my son?

87
00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:09.040
-Yeah...
-Yeah.

88
00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:10.459
<i>I asked...</i>

89
00:04:10.542 --> 00:04:13.712
how many of you here
<i>loved my son?!</i>

90
00:04:16.882 --> 00:04:19.509
Maybe you loved him
because he was a leader.

91
00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:22.179
a scholar. an athlete.

92
00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:26.141
I loved him because he was <i>mine.</i>

93
00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:28.101
Because he was my son.

94
00:04:28.185 --> 00:04:29.352
We love you. Mort!

95
00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:31.146
Mort! Mort! Mort! Mort!

96
00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:36.234
When I die. I will
kill God for taking my boy!

97
00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.946
I don't approve of your promise.

98
00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:41.239
but I understand.

99
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.661
Who will be there for me
now that you're gone?

100
00:04:49.247 --> 00:04:50.683
Chesterfield?

101
00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:52.250
Oh. oh!
No. no. no. no. no. no!

102
00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.461
Oh!
Stop. stop!

103
00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:56.254
Mort?

104
00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.757
Oh... no...

105
00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.259
You guys have never
seen another Morty before?

106
00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:02.761
Oh!

107
00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:04.054
Oh!

108
00:05:04.095 --> 00:05:05.847
Does that make sense?

109
00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:09.476
S-shortest version is...
infinite me's. infinite you's.

110
00:05:09.559 --> 00:05:10.644
You want a grilled cheese?

111
00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:12.229
I want to make it for him.

112
00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.313
And this thing?

113
00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:14.396
It's how I got here.

114
00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:15.607
Rick made it for me.

115
00:05:15.649 --> 00:05:18.860
Not my Rick...
i-it's a lot of canon.

116
00:05:18.944 --> 00:05:20.362
Where is Rick?

117
00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:21.822
I'm sorry to tell you this.

118
00:05:21.905 --> 00:05:23.406
but. um...

119
00:05:23.448 --> 00:05:25.116
our Rick...

120
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.786
is a drunk. Morty.

121
00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:30.413
Ohh... No?

122
00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:32.290
We had to end our
relationship with him.

123
00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:33.708
We tried everything to help.

124
00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.460
but ultimately.
he needed to help himself.

125
00:05:35.502 --> 00:05:37.337
And he. like. listened?

126
00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.047
This universe <i>is</i> wild.

127
00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.340
Just the way you like it.

128
00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:41.925
Mmm.

129
00:05:41.967 --> 00:05:43.718
Wow. So good.

130
00:05:43.802 --> 00:05:45.720
Don't suppose
there's any tomato soup...

131
00:05:45.804 --> 00:05:46.638
Holy shit.

132
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.223
You guys are something else.

133
00:05:48.306 --> 00:05:49.766
You should have met our Mort.

134
00:05:50.517 --> 00:05:52.352
<i>Ray. like it or not...</i>

135
00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:54.813
Mm. <i>...the bank's
gonna take your farm.</i>

136
00:05:54.855 --> 00:05:56.439
<i>They will come. Ray.</i>

137
00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:58.066
Huh?
Oh. my gosh.

138
00:05:58.108 --> 00:05:59.818
My family's probably worried.

139
00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.404
My... other family.
You're leaving?

140
00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:04.322
Summer. he's not ours to keep.

141
00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:05.824
I understand. Mort...

142
00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:07.450
I mean. Morty.

143
00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.412
Come back to us. kiddo.

144
00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:12.831
Whenever you want.
you come back.

145
00:06:16.835 --> 00:06:19.588
Summer.
stop live-streaming!

146
00:06:24.926 --> 00:06:26.136
Where have you been?

147
00:06:26.177 --> 00:06:27.977
I've needed you to hand me
wrenches and stuff.

148
00:06:28.013 --> 00:06:29.514
Check this out.

149
00:06:29.598 --> 00:06:30.974
Wow. great.

150
00:06:31.016 --> 00:06:32.976
Huh? Ah!
Oh. Rick!

151
00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:34.352
It's pulling my insides!

152
00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.788
You have too much
metal in you dipshit.

153
00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:37.397
Oh!

154
00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.566
I didn't put it there.
So?

155
00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.868
Oh. hey!
Hey!

156
00:06:49.951 --> 00:06:51.470
Morty. you came back!

157
00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:53.371
Oh. geez. G-Good boy.

158
00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.332
That's a dog for ya.

159
00:06:55.373 --> 00:06:57.042
M-my dog enslaved me.

160
00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:58.418
B-but not this one.

161
00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.003
So I'm hanging out
of the side

162
00:07:00.045 --> 00:07:01.212
of the ship in space.

163
00:07:01.296 --> 00:07:02.756
holding the guitar
that Rick wanted.

164
00:07:02.839 --> 00:07:04.483
but my eyes burst from
the pressure difference

165
00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:06.051
and I couldn't see
for. like. an hour.

166
00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.219
Morty.
you could have been killed.

167
00:07:08.303 --> 00:07:10.513
Oh. yeah. I was.

168
00:07:10.555 --> 00:07:11.640
You <i>died?</i>

169
00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:13.433
You die. and come back?

170
00:07:13.516 --> 00:07:15.226
The worst part
is waking up in the tube.

171
00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.020
where the fresh body is

172
00:07:17.062 --> 00:07:19.439
c-cause you have to cough all
that fluid out of your lungs.

173
00:07:19.522 --> 00:07:21.566
You're saying
where you come from.

174
00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.904
your grandfather lets you die
over and over again?

175
00:07:25.946 --> 00:07:28.239
What does your father
say about this?

176
00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.367
♪ Who's a Mad Men? ♪

177
00:07:30.408 --> 00:07:32.702
♪ I'm a Mad Men ♪

178
00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:38.750
Oh. my God.
I <i>made</i> an owl.

179
00:07:38.792 --> 00:07:40.085
T-this is incredible.

180
00:07:40.168 --> 00:07:42.545
Too bad my big lathe
is up at the cabin.

181
00:07:42.587 --> 00:07:44.381
Built it with my dad.

182
00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:45.757
Then Mort helped me put up

183
00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.425
the sleeping porch
just last summer.

184
00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:49.260
Wish we could take you
there this weekend.

185
00:07:49.344 --> 00:07:51.447
but the gals are going to be
at the soup kitchen and...

186
00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.682
I mean. <i>we</i> could head up there.

187
00:07:53.765 --> 00:07:54.933
just the two of us?

188
00:07:55.016 --> 00:07:57.435
Really?
You'd want to do that?

189
00:08:06.569 --> 00:08:07.862
Don't you have any matches?

190
00:08:07.946 --> 00:08:09.656
A man who relies on matches

191
00:08:09.739 --> 00:08:11.658
gets pretty cold
when he runs out.

192
00:08:13.368 --> 00:08:14.703
You feel like a steak?

193
00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:20.083
Wait till the pan
releases the meat.

194
00:08:24.754 --> 00:08:28.842
I feel like I've
never learned anything until now.

195
00:08:29.926 --> 00:08:33.304
And Mort. he's climbing so fast.

196
00:08:33.388 --> 00:08:34.639
When he loses his footing.

197
00:08:34.723 --> 00:08:36.850
he's just silent as he falls...

198
00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:39.352
until the crack
of his body hitting stone.

199
00:08:41.312 --> 00:08:42.856
Mort was so strong.

200
00:08:42.939 --> 00:08:44.941
but I wasn't strong enough
to save him.

201
00:08:44.983 --> 00:08:47.485
I'm so sorry.

202
00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.487
I know you're not my Mort...

203
00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:51.197
Not really...

204
00:08:51.948 --> 00:08:54.242
but I love you just the same.

205
00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:56.745
I-I love you. dad.

206
00:08:56.828 --> 00:08:58.788
I-I want to be your son.

207
00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.124
I <i>am</i> your son.

208
00:09:05.336 --> 00:09:06.671
Then break the gun.

209
00:09:07.172 --> 00:09:09.674
What? This isn't one
of your adventures.

210
00:09:09.716 --> 00:09:11.634
It can be your life.

211
00:09:11.676 --> 00:09:13.011
But what if I need to...

212
00:09:13.053 --> 00:09:14.596
What could you need
that isn't here?

213
00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.222
A family that
doesn't appreciate you?

214
00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:18.349
A resurrection machine that
makes infinite grandpas?

215
00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:21.144
You need to turn into
a fucking giraffe?

216
00:09:21.186 --> 00:09:22.812
Do it!

217
00:09:22.854 --> 00:09:24.147
Uh...

218
00:09:24.189 --> 00:09:25.398
Hey!

219
00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:28.026
Oh. my God!

220
00:09:28.068 --> 00:09:30.612
Yes! I love you!

221
00:09:30.653 --> 00:09:33.364
I tried to make my son strong.

222
00:09:33.448 --> 00:09:35.617
So strong he would never die!

223
00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.702
Ah!

224
00:09:45.001 --> 00:09:47.587
I just want to keep you safe!

225
00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.297
Mort?

226
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.548
Mort.

227
00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.092
Mort?

228
00:09:53.051 --> 00:09:54.052
Mort!

229
00:09:54.636 --> 00:09:56.346
Come back.

230
00:10:01.142 --> 00:10:03.728
<i>Dad wants me
to free solo El Capitan.</i>

231
00:10:03.812 --> 00:10:05.355
<i>He's crazy.</i>

232
00:10:05.396 --> 00:10:07.398
<i>He wants me to be able
to survive anything.</i>

233
00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.067
<i>My only hope's to run away.</i>

234
00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:11.194
Thank you. Mort.

235
00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:45.895
And we're left with
a radical non-duality.

236
00:10:45.937 --> 00:10:48.106
The universe is
not locally real.

237
00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:50.775
Which means nothing matters...

238
00:10:50.817 --> 00:10:53.778
or <i>everything</i> does.

239
00:10:54.904 --> 00:10:56.990
Moral universe. let's go!

240
00:10:58.366 --> 00:10:59.450
I fucking knew it.

241
00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:00.702
The Central Finite Curve.

242
00:11:00.785 --> 00:11:01.995
portal travel. all of it.

243
00:11:02.078 --> 00:11:03.788
Of course there's
infinite Mortys...

244
00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:05.874
because there's
infinite worlds. Morty.

245
00:11:05.957 --> 00:11:07.709
<i>and</i> infinite me's!

246
00:11:07.792 --> 00:11:09.544
A-am I cool in most worlds?

247
00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:11.462
Oh!
Mr. Sanchez?

248
00:11:11.546 --> 00:11:13.590
Oh. sorry I frighten you.

249
00:11:13.631 --> 00:11:15.133
I am from Russia.

250
00:11:15.842 --> 00:11:17.427
Who is hunting you?

251
00:11:17.468 --> 00:11:19.679
Jerry? I don't know.
Ma-maybe all of them?

252
00:11:19.762 --> 00:11:21.014
I just want to go home.

253
00:11:21.097 --> 00:11:22.366
I thought there
was a better version

254
00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:24.934
of my family for me.
but I was wrong.

255
00:11:24.976 --> 00:11:26.728
Do you think
you could make this?

256
00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:28.980
Oh. Morty.
I would love to help you.

257
00:11:29.063 --> 00:11:31.608
but that thing
almost destroyed me.

258
00:11:31.649 --> 00:11:34.152
Salieri to infinite Mozarts.

259
00:11:34.944 --> 00:11:36.779
Do... Do you guys
not have Mozart?

260
00:11:36.821 --> 00:11:39.282
Oh. Morty.
we gotta watch "Amadeus."

261
00:11:39.324 --> 00:11:40.575
Shit. I'm late.

262
00:11:40.658 --> 00:11:41.784
I gotta do a thing.

263
00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:43.786
Uh. do you wanna come with me?

264
00:11:43.828 --> 00:11:45.246
Ahem.

265
00:11:45.288 --> 00:11:46.915
